==Changes 2022–2023==
In August 2022, six Conservative councillors left the party to sit as independents, being Michelle Cook (elected 2019), Danny Cook, Peter Thurgood and John Wade (all elected 2021), and Rosey Claymore and Ben Price (both elected 2022).<ref>{{cite news |last1=Newbould |first1=Daniel |title=Six councillors resign from Conservative party of Tamworth Borough Council - full statements |url=https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/news/midlands-news/six-councillors-resign-conservative-party-24709388 |access-date=31 December 2023 |work=Birmingham Live |date=9 August 2022}}</ref>

